# assert-hygiene allowlist — see AGENTS.md §9.2 and
# docs/architecture/failure-model.md §5.
#
# Format: one fnmatch glob per line (matched against the repo-relative path);
# an optional `# reason` documents WHY the path may add assert-family lines.
# Blank lines and full-line comments are ignored.
#
# Auto-allowed WITHOUT an entry here: added lines that sit inside an active
# SLUICE_ASYNC_INTERNAL_TESTING preprocessor guard (category 3,
# internal-testing preconditions) — detected mechanically in the new-file
# content by scripts/gates/assert-hygiene.py. The #else/#elif branch of such
# a guard is production code and is NOT auto-allowed.
#
# The gate is changed-lines only: pre-existing sites elsewhere are
# grandfathered (backlog: issue #144). This file is for NEW lines.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Category 1 — Completion L9 pattern (Debug tripwire layered on a Release
# path that already returns the documented typed error; Release is correct
# without the assert):
include/sluice/async/completion.hpp  # Completion L9: assert + Release invalid_state fallback (header contract §L9)
#
# Category 2 — pure diagnostics (assert observes an invariant proven
# elsewhere; its failure changes no returned value or state transition).
# No permanent entries; add case-by-case with a written reason.
#
# Category 3 — internal-testing preconditions inside guarded seams are
# auto-allowed via guard detection; whole-file entries for seam headers that
# are not self-guarded may be added here after PR
# agent/internal-test-control-plane (#145) lands, if needed.
